 ## Overview
-PCA Pose Alignment transforms a set of camera-to-world poses so that the principal components of their translation vectors lie on the XYZ axes [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It re-centers the poses, rotates them based on the eigenvectors of the covariance matrix, ensures a consistent coordinate system orientation, and scales them to fit within the $[-1, 1]^3$ cube [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Sim(3) Alignment via Procrustes Analysis](8526-sim-3-alignment-via-procrustes-analysis.md) which aligns poses using Procrustes analysis [S1, unofficial].
+PCA Pose Alignment transforms a set of camera-to-world poses so that the principal components of their translation vectors lie on the XYZ axes [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It re-centers the poses, rotates them based on the eigenvectors of the covariance matrix, ensures a consistent coordinate system orientation, and scales them to fit within the $[-1, 1]^3$ cube [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Sim(3) Alignment via Procrustes Analysis](8526-sim-3-alignment-via-procrustes-analysis.md), which aligns poses using Procrustes analysis rather than PCA on translation vectors [G].
 
